The manifest compiled without the sandbox, but my regex literal `/#([\w-]+)/` is being
 parsed as a key path because of the `#` after the `/`. In Swift, when a `/` is followed
 by `#` (or when the first character is `#`), it gets parsed as a key path (like `
#keyPath`) instead of a regex literal. To use a `#` in a regex literal, you need to
 put a space after the opening `/`. That is, you need to write it as `/ #([\w-]+)/
`.
