SE-0356: extended regex literals. In multi-line literals (using indentation), the
 closing delimiter's indentation determines what gets stripped. For single-line, the
 literal is everything between the slashes. So `/ #([\w-]+)/` = pattern " #([\w-]+
)" — with a leading space. That would fail on "shopping list,#urgent." — no wait,
 "list,#urgent." — there's a space before "#urgent", so " #urgent" would match. But
 "(#ideas)" has no space before #ideas — it wouldn't match!

