NSRegularExpression approach:

```swift
import Foundation

public func extractTags(from text: String) -> [String] {
    let pattern = try! NSRegularExpression(pattern: "#(\\w|-)+")
    let ns = text as NSString
    return pattern.matches(in: text, range: NSRange(location: 0, length: ns.length
))
        .compactMap { ns.substring(with: $0.range(at: 1)) }
}
```

Hmm, capture group `(\w|-)+`. In NSRegularExpression (ICU syntax), `\w` is word characters
. Group 1 is the tag name. Order of matches is preserved.

